        <description>LEAP BORESCOPE INSPECTION TASKS -  REQUIRED EVERY 1600FC
PARTNO : CFMLEAP-1B / SERIALNO : 60A198
         ENGINE CFM LEAP-1B
         POS: #2


*** CRITICAL TASK ***

NOTE 1: THIS IS A CRITICAL TASK AS PER 145.A.48. AN INDEPENDENT INSPECTION MUST BE ACCOMPLISHED TO ENSURE THE SATISFACTORY COMPLETION OF THE TASK AND THAT NO DEFICIENCIES HAVE BEEN FOUND.

NOTE 2: THIS INSPECTION IS NORMALLY ACCOMPLISHED AS AN "OUT OF PHASE TASK" ON EACH INDIVIDUAL ENGINE.

NOTE 3: EACH BORESCOPE PLUG MUST BE IDENTIFIED AT REMOVAL TO ENSURE IT IS RE-INSTALLED IN ITS CORRECT POSITION. IF THERE IS DOUBT ABOUT THE POSITION OF A BORESCOPE PLUG THE IPC MUST BE CONSULTED TO VERIFY ITS POSITION.

NOTE 4: INDEPENDENT INSPECTION MUST BE ACCOMPLISHED TO ENSURE ALL BORESCOPE INSPECTION PORTS AND THE HAND CRANKING COVER ARE INSTALLED CORRECTLY AND ENGINE/AIRFRAME IS RESTORED TO NORMAL.

NOTE 5: IF THIS TASK IS BEING ACCOMPLISHED ON BOTH ENGINES AT THE SAME TIME THE INITIAL INSPECTION MUST BE ACCOMPLISHED BY A DIFFERENT PERSON TO THE INDEPENDENT INSPECTION. IT IS ACCEPTABLE FOR TWO PEOPLE TO REVERSE THEIR ROLES IN THIS INSTANCE, WHEREBY THE PERSON WHO DOES THE INITIAL TASK ON ONE ENGINE MAY DO THE INDEPENDENT INSPECTION ON THE SECOND ENGINE AND VICE-VERSA.

NOTE 6: A TECH LOG ENTRY IS TO BE MADE REFERENCING THIS WO.

ACTION:

NOTE 7: FOR STEP 1 AND 2 AMM 72-00-00-290-805-G00 APPLIES. IF RIGID SCOPE IS BEING USED FOR INSPECTION BORESCOPE INSPECTION OF THE COMBUSTION CHAMBER AND FUEL NOZZLES MUST BE CARRIED OUT THROUGH BOTH PORTS (N AND O) AND BOTH IGNITER PORTS  

NOTE 8: IF FINDINGS ARE DISCOVERED DURING THE ACCOMPLISHMENT OF RIGID BORESCOPE, PERFORM A FULL 360 DEGREE FLEX BORESCOPE THROUGH ANY OF THE APPLICABLE PORTS.

1. CARRY OUT AMP 72-220-01-01/02-01, 72-225-01-01/02-01, 72-230-01-01/02-01, 72-235-01-01/ 02-01 RELATED TO BORESCOPE INSPECTION OF THE COMBUSTION CHAMBER.

IF INSPECTION IS ON LH ENGINE: BOEING TASK CARD 72-220-01-01, 72-225-01-01, 72-230-01-01, 72-235-01-01 REFERS
IF INSPECTION IS ON RH ENGINE: BOEING TASK CARD 72-220-02-01, 72-225-02-01, 72-230-02-01, 72-235-02-01 REFERS

2.  CARRY OUT AMP 73-030-01-01/02-01 RELATED TO BORESCOPE INSPECTION OF THE FUEL NOZZLES 

IF INSPECTION IS ON LH ENGINE: BOEING TASK CARD 73-030-01-01 REFERS
IF INSPECTION IS ON RH ENGINE: BOEING TASK CARD 73-030-02-01 REFERS

NOTE 9: STEP 3 AND STEP 4 MUST BE ACCCOMPLISHED BY USING AMM 72-00-00-290-806-G00. 

3. CARRY OUT AMP 72-240-01-01/02-01 RELATED TO BORESCOPE INSPECTION OF THE ENGINE STAGE 1 HPT BLADES.

IF INSPECTION IS ON LH ENGINE: BOEING TASK CARD 72-240-01-01 REFERS
IF INSPECTION IS ON RH ENGINE: BOEING TASK CARD 72-240-02-01 REFERS

4. CARRY OUT AMP 72-245-01-01/02-01 RELATED TO BORESCOPE INSPECTION OF THE ENGINE STAGE 2 HPT BLADES.

IF INSPECTION IS ON LH ENGINE: BOEING TASK CARD 72-245-01-01 REFERS
IF INSPECTION IS ON RH ENGINE: BOEING TASK CARD 72-245-02-01 REFERS

NOTE 10: AMP TASKCARD 72-250-01-01, 72-250-02-01, 72-260-01-01 &amp; 72-260-02-01 ARE SATISFIED THROUGH ACCOMPLISHMENT OF STEP 3 AND 4 OF THIS WORKORDER. BOEING MESSAGE RYR-RYR-22-0739-04B(R1) REFERS.

5. CLEARLY STATE IN THE CLOSURE / ACTION SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER IF THERE IS ANY EVIDENCE OF ASH DEPOSITS, COOLING HOLE PLUGGING, UNUSUAL OVER-TEMPERATURE, UNUSUAL OXIDATION, UNUSUAL CRACK, MISSING MATERIAL, TEAR OR BURNING, FOUND IN THE HIGH PRESSURE TURBINE (HPT). IF THERE IS EVIDENCE, INFORM POWERPLANT@RYANAIR.COM AND FOLLOW AMM LIMITS FOR CONTINUED OPERATION.

6. CARRY OUT  TEST 4 - AN IDLE-POWER LEAK CHECK IAW AMM TASK 71-00-00-790-804-G00 AND CERTIFY FOR IT IN THE CLOSURE / ACTION SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER.

7. IF INSPECTION IS PERFORMED BY GE/SAFRAN OR ANY OTHER THIRD PARTY;

A) DO NOT CERTIFY ANY THIRD-PARTY PAPERWORK, IF THERE ARE OPEN ITEMS ON THE THEIR CARRY FORWARD SHEET TRANSFER AND CERTIFY FOR THEM IN THE CLOSURE / ACTION SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER.

B) IF GE/SAFRAN OR ANY OTHER THIRD PARTY CARRIED OUT THE REQUIRED INDEPENDENT INSPECTIONS, CLEARLY STATE THIS IN THE CLOSURE / ACTION SECTION OF THIS WORK ORDER AND ATTACH THEIR FORM 1.

*** CRITICAL TASK ***
THIS IS A CRITICAL TASK AS PER 145.A.48. AN INDEPENDENT INSPECTION MUST BE ACCOMPLISHED TO ENSURE THE SATISFACTORY COMPLETION OF THE TASK AND THAT NO DEFICIENCIES HAVE BEEN FOUND.

PERFORM INITIAL INSPECTION:

SIGN ______________________ DATE _________ TIME ___________ AUTH ____________

PERFORM INDEPENDENT INSPECTION:

SIGN ______________________ DATE _________ TIME ___________ AUTH ____________</description>
